    "done_when": "Read plan artifacts-carry-no-worktree-paths sections 1, 3, 4 and 5 first, and the landed section 2 record; section 3 and 4 are the specification and this text restates only their measures. At the dispatch base 6277209bc the census `git grep -l -I 'reckon-worktrees' HEAD -- . ':!docs/plans' ':!docs/state' ':!docs/research'` lists 71 files: 66 launch scripts (.sh, .sbatch, .py), five data files the section 2 rule left unmapped, and nova/database/filepath.py, which is exempt. (1) Each launch script is read: where the worktree path is one the script uses, it resolves its repository root at run time with the realpath-first idiom of scripts/nova_lane/run.sh in shell, or git rev-parse --show-toplevel run from Path(__file__).resolve().parent in Python; where the path is only a comment or echoed banner, the file goes through `filepath relativize`. benchmarks/backend_divergence_forensics.py and benchmarks/pure_arm_comparison_figure.py import WORKTREE_ROOT from nova.database.filepath instead of spelling the root. (2) The five unmapped data files: reword the two docs/evidence/fragments/figure-and-solver-audit fragments and docs/evidence/replan-2026-09-24/thin-interfaces.md so they describe worktree paths without spelling the root, and repair by hand the truncated path in docs/evidence/archive/cpu-compile-abort-landed.html and the space-broken path in docs/evidence/archive/figure-and-solver-audit-landed.html to repository-relative form, changing nothing else in those records. (3) Add a --check mode to the relativize subcommand in nova/database/scripts.py that reads the staged files from the index and exits nonzero naming each offender returned by worktree_path_offenders. Add tests/test_artifacts_carry_no_worktree_paths.py, which lists tracked files with git ls-files, passes them to worktree_path_offenders with a working-tree reader, fails naming each offender, and has a positive control proving it reaches a file in every top-level directory. Delete test_no_rece